Package: isolatr
Title: Simulate and Evaluate Quarantine Testing Strategies for COVID-19
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R: 
    person("Kylie", "Ainslie", , "k.ainslie@unimelb.edu.au", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0001-5419-7206"))
Description: Provides tools for simulating COVID-19 transmission dynamics during
    quarantine and evaluating the effectiveness of different testing strategies.
    The package implements a stochastic simulation model that accounts for household
    structure, vaccination status, isolation timing, and various Test-Trace-Isolate-Quarantine
    (TTIQ) scenarios. It enables users to compare testing schedules and quantify their
    impact on reducing onwards transmission from quarantined individuals.
